T11:32:34.138597"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-08-17T11:32:34.138597"}}},"ISBN:9781573226103":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781573226103","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL22578823M/Kitchen_table_wisdom","preview":"restricted","preview_url":"https://archive.org/details/kitchentablewis100reme","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6894396-S.jpg","details":{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["104533"],"librarything":["42829"]},"title":"Kitchen table wisdom","subtitle":"stories that heal","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL528208A","name":"Rachel Naomi Remen"}],"publish_date":"1997","publishers":["Riverhead Books","Riverhead Trade"],"ia_box_id":["IA141611"],"covers":[6894396],"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:O7-AVT-448","urn:sfpl:31223114498430","urn:cst:10011460589","urn:bwbsku:O7-APX-820","urn:bwbsku:O7-ADT-930","urn:bwbsku:O7-DSS-403","urn:bwbsku:O7-BGM-896","urn:bwbsku:W6-AFY-025","urn:bwbsku:W6-AOR-010"],"lc_classifications":["R154.R374 A3 1996"],"ocaid":"kitchentablewis100reme","publish_places":["New York"],"subjects":["Remen, Rachel Naomi.","Remen, Rachel Naomi -- Philosophy.","Physicians -- United States -- Biography.","Meditations."],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"xxxii, 336 p. ;","source_records":["promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-04-06:O7-AVT-448","ia:kitchentablewis100reme","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run02.mrc:160078651:1238","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_barcode.mrc:222726723:5992","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_multibarcode.mrc:223000798:5992","bwb:9781573226103","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-03-08:O7-APX-820","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-03-08:O7-ADT-930","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-03-08:O7-DSS-403","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2021-01-29:O7-BGM-896","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-10-20:W6-AFY-025","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-10-20:W6-AOR-010","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_031.bib.mrc:97131160:8192","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_041.bib.mrc:286409944:3082"],"dewey_decimal_class":["610/.92","B"],"edition_name":"1st Riverhead trade paperback ed.","isbn_10":["1573226106"],"publish_country":"nyu","by_statement":"Rachel Naomi Remen ; foreword by Dean Ornish.","type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lccn":["96005175"],"key":"/books/OL22578823M","number_of_pages":336,"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3240345W"}],"oclc_numbers":["34243379","37367251"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"Everybody is a story,\" writes Dr. Remen in her introduction. \"When I was a child, people sat around kitchen tables and told their stories. We don't do that so much anymore. Sitting around the table telling stories is not just a way of passing time. It is the way the wisdom gets passed along. The stuff that helps us to live a life worth remembering. Despite the awesome powers of technology many of us still do not live very well. We may need to listen to one another's.\n\nStories again.\" Loneliness is the hidden wound of our time, the price many have paid for embracing such frontier values as independence, self-reliance, and competence. Rachel Remen invites us to see below the surface and remember that we are connected and can become one another's healers. Dr. Remen's unique and intimate relationship with healing and the life force comes from her experience as a physician, a professor of medicine, a therapist, and a long-term survivor of.\n\nChronic illness. Her stories, picked from the tree of life, are dedicated to the ordinary hero in all of us and stand witness to life's natural tendency to heal our wounds. In these remarkable parables, we discover that our goal in life might not be a precise destination, but the ability to travel together with humor and meaning, with purpose and quality companionship, with warmth and tenderness. Kitchen Table Wisdom shows us that a good story is like a compass for.\n\nLife's journey, and reminds us of the power and joy of being fully human."},"latest_revision":28,"revision":28,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-11-16T13:41:19.690330"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-06-28T23:46:00.867458"}}},"ISBN:9781101655238":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781101655238","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL50501722M/Kitchen_Table_Wisdom","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL50501722M/Kitchen_Table_Wisdom","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL528208A","name":"Rachel Naomi Remen"}],"isbn_13":["9781101655238"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"number_of_pages":379,"publish_date":"2006","publishers":["Riverhead Books"],"source_records":["idb:9781101655238"],"subjects":["Motivational & inspirational","Inspiration & personal growth","Death, grief, bereavement","General interests & hobbies -> self-help -> self-help general","General interests & hobbies -> body, mind, spirit -> body, mind, spirit"],"title":"Kitchen Table Wisdom","subtitle":"Stories that Heal, 10th Anniversary Edition","full_title":"Kitchen Table Wisdom Stories that Heal, 10th Anniversary Edition","works":[{"key":"/works/OL3240345W"}],"key":"/books/OL50501722M","latest_revision":1,"revision":1,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-12-20T01:08:54.688206"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2023-12-20T01:08:54.688206"}}},"ISBN:9781597770996":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781597770996","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9838559M/Kitchen_Table_Wisdom","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL9838559M/Kitchen_Table_Wisdom","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/2000802-S.jpg","details":{"identifiers":{"goodreads":["7119332"]},"title":"Kitchen Table Wisdom","subtitle":"Stories That Heal","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL528208A","name":"Rachel Naomi Remen"}],"publish_date":"July 1, 2006","publishers":["Phoenix Audio"],"weight":"4 ounces","covers":[2000802],"physical_format":"Audio CD","subjects":["Religion","Abridged Audi